cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "UBDS — Universal Brine Dispersion Solver"
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying case study, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Onyejekwe
    given-names: Akosa Samuel
    email: samuelonyejekwe852@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/samuelakosaonyejekwe/brine-dispersion-analysis-sam"
abstract: >-
  UBDS is an open, physics-based solver that unifies the near-, medium- and
  far-field dispersion of brine and other buoyant or negatively buoyant
  effluents in a single dynamically-coupled, mass-conserving framework: a
  sign-agnostic Lagrangian integral jet/plume model, a 2-D depth-averaged
  shallow-water hydrodynamic engine, and a quasi-3D sigma-layer
  advection-dispersion engine with a dense-water gravity-current closure. The
  repository includes the Bahia Azul desalination brine-outfall case study,
  built entirely on synthetic but physically credible site data.
keywords:
  - brine dispersion
  - desalination
  - outfall
  - hydrodynamics
  - plume model
  - shallow water equations
  - environmental modelling
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-10"
